ific features, so that only pods that request those features can be scheduled on those nodes.\n\n[D3] You also need a plugin for NFD that adds appropriate labels to your nodes; these might be generic\nlabels or they could be vendor specific. Your GPU vendor may provide a third party\nplugin for NFD; check their documentation for more details.\n\nClaim:\nFor our proposed NFD deployment, NFD can be used both to advertise detected node features as node labels and to taint those nodes so that only pods requesting those features are scheduled on them.\n\nProposed answer:\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"supported\",\n  \"evidence\": [\"D1\", \"D2\"]\n}\n\nAudit JSON:",
